  "tolerance_note": "Every numeric quantity carries its own tolerance; lengths are in metres in the IFC project coordinate system (no georeferencing). Alignment coordinates and pier positions are exact to the closed forms within 1e-6 m; the deck bounding box uses 0.05 m to cover the 10 m chord approximation of the curved 10 m band.",
  "computation": {
    "horizontal": "x(s) and y(s) are the closed-form integrals of cos(heading) and sin(heading): a straight line for 0..100, x = 100 + R sin((s-100)/R) and y = R (1 - cos((s-100)/R)) for the 200 m left arc, then a straight line at heading 0.5 rad. Checked against composite 8-point Gauss-Legendre integration with 10 m intervals (agreement better than 1e-9 m). Nothing uses IfcOpenShell geometry.",
    "vertical": "The vertical layout is a single constant 0 % gradient, so z(s) = 0 everywhere.",
    "deck": "One IfcSectionedSolidHorizontal on the horizontal IfcCompositeCurve: a 10.00 x 1.00 m rectangle profile with its top at the alignment elevation, cross-sections every 10 m from 0 to 400 m. Each IfcAxis2PlacementLinear sets Axis to global up and RefDirection to the horizontal left normal, because IFC 4.3 defines the profile X axis as RefDirection and the profile Y axis as Axis. Volume = 10 x 1 x 400 = 4000 m3 ideal; the chord approximation of the 200 m arc gives about 3999.87 m3.",
    "deck_bbox": "A constant-width band swept along the alignment has its extreme plan coordinates on one of its two edge curves. Both edges are sampled every 0.1 m; the 0.05 m tolerance covers the 10 m chord sagitta (about 0.031 m at R = 405 m).",
    "piers": "Each pier is an IfcColumn with a 2 x 2 m rectangle profile extruded 8 m along local +Z. Its object placement puts the local origin at the alignment point on the pier station, z = -9, with local X along the tangent, so the pier is yawed by the alignment heading. The axis-aligned bbox half extents of a 2 x 2 square yawed by h are |cos h| + |sin h| in both X and Y.",
    "counts": "Counts of the entities authored below."
  },
